The graph of $y=ax^2+bx+c$ is given below, where $a$, $b$, and $c$ are integers.  Find $a-b+c$.

[asy]
size(150);

Label f;

f.p=fontsize(4);

xaxis(-3,3,Ticks(f, 1.0));

yaxis(-4,4,Ticks(f, 1.0));

real f(real x)

{

return x^2+2x-1;

}

draw(graph(f,-2.7,.7),linewidth(1),Arrows(6));
[/asy]

accepted_response:
First, we compute the value inside 7 function evaluations,
\begin{align*}
&f(19) \\
&= 19+2 \\
&= 21 \\
\end{align*}

\begin{align*}
&g(f(19)) \\
&= g(21) \\
&= 21/3 \\
&= 7.
\end{align*}

\begin{align*}
&f^{-1}(7) \\
&= 7-2 \\
&= 5.
\end{align*}

\begin{align*}
&f^{-1}(5) \\
&= 3.
\end{align*}

\begin{align*}
&g^{-1}(3) \\
&= 3\cdot 3 \\
&= 9
\end{align*}

\begin{align*}
&f(g^{-1}(f^{-1}(f^{-1}(g(f(19)))))) \\
&= f(9) \\
&= \boxed{11}.
\end{align*}
</think> <answer>11</answer>

