question:
For some constants $a$ and $b,$ let \[f(x) = \left\{
\begin{array}{cl}
ax + b & \text{if } x < 2, \\
8 - 3x & \text{if } x \ge 2.
\end{array}
\right.\]The function $f$ has the property that $f(f(x)) = x$ for all $x.$ What is $a + b?$

accepted_response:
Setting $x=2,$ we have \[f(f(2)) = f(8 - 3 \cdot 2) = f(2)=2.\]This means that $a\cdot 2 + b = 2.$ Setting $x=a\cdot 2 + b,$ we have \[f(f(a\cdot 2 + b)) = f(a\cdot (a \cdot 2 + b) + b) = f(8 - 3\cdot (a \cdot 2 + b)) = a \cdot (8 - 3 \cdot (a \cdot 2 + b)) + b.\]Using the fact that $f(f(x)) = x$ for all $x,$ we have  \[a \cdot (8 - 3 \cdot (a \cdot 2 + b)) + b = a \cdot 2 + b.\][asy]
draw((0,-1)--(0,2));
draw((0,0)--(6,0));
draw((2,1.95)--(2,-2.05));
label("$x$", (6,0.05), E);
