label("y=x", (4,4), N);
label("y=8-3x", (2,-3), E);
label("$y = ax+b$", (4,-1.05), S);
[/asy]Moving everything around, we have $a(8-6a-3b)=0,$ so either $a=0$ or $a=\frac{4-3b}{3}.$  If $a=0,$ then $b=2,$ so $a+b=2.$ If $a \ne 0,$ then $4-3b=0,$ so $b=\frac{4}{3}$ and $a=1,$ so $a+b=\boxed{\frac{7}{3}}.$
