Now we plug in $y=4$ and solve for $z$: \begin{align*} k &= y^3 \cdot \sqrt[3]{z} \\ 8 &= 4^3 \cdot \sqrt[3]{z} \\ 8 &= 64 \cdot \sqrt[3]{z} \\ \sqrt[3]{z} &= \frac{8}{64} = \frac{1}{8} \\ z &= \boxed{\frac{1}{512}}. \\ \end{align*}
