Suppose $\angle ABP = \angle PBQ = \angle QBK = x$. Also suppose $\angle MBQ = y$. $BM$ bisects $\angle PBQ$ so $ \angle MBP = \angle MBQ = y$.

Thus,
\begin{align*}
\angle ABQ &= 2x \\
\angle MBQ &= y \\
\angle MBP & =   y
\end{align*}
Therefore, \begin{align*}
\frac{\angle MBQ}{\angle FBQ} &= \frac{y}{2x} \\
&= \frac{y}{4y} \\
&=\boxed{\frac{1}{4}}.
\end{align*}
