question:
Find the least positive four-digit solution to the following system of congruences. \begin{align*}
7x &\equiv 21 \pmod{14} \\
2x+13 &\equiv 16 \pmod{9} \\
-2x+1 &\equiv x \pmod{25} \\
\end{align*}

accepted_response:
We convert to base 10 for computation and then back to base 7.  We have \begin{align*}
24_7 &= 2\cdot7 + 4 = 18 = 24_{10}\\
30_7 &= 3\cdot7 + 0 = 21 = 21_{10}
\end{align*}Therefore, $24_7\cdot 30_7 = 24_{10}\cdot 21_{10} = 504_{10}$.  Now we convert this to base 7.

\begin{align*}
504/7 &= 72 &\text{which leaves a remainder of 0}\\
72/7 &= 10 &\text{which leaves a remainder of 2}\\
10/7 &= 1 &\text{which leaves a remainder of 3}\\
1/7 &= 0 &\text{which leaves a remainder of 1}
\end{align*}So $504_{10} = 1320_7$.  The sum of the digits of this number is $1+3+2+0 = \boxed{6}$.
</think> <answer>6</answer>

