accepted_response:
The area of the larger square is $7^2=49$ square units; the area of the smaller square is $3^2=9$ square units. [asy]
fill((0,0)--(1,0)--(1,1)--(0,1)--cycle,black);
fill((9,0)--(9+6,0)--(9+6,6)--(9,6)--cycle,white);
gment((0.5,0.5),abs(6));
segment((0.5,0.5),abs(8.66025403784));
[/asy] Thus there are $49-9=\boxed{40}$ square units in the black region.
