Since $\overline{BC}$ is the altitude to the hypotenuse of $\triangle ABC,$ calculations of area give us
\[\frac{1}{2} \cdot 20 \cdot 15 = \frac{1}{2} \cdot 15 \cdot h \Rightarrow h = 20,\]so $\overline{AC} = \sqrt{20^2 - 15^2} = 5\sqrt{7}.$

Thus,
\begin{align*}
\tan A &= \frac{\overline{BC}}{\overline{AB}} = \frac{15}{5\sqrt{7}} = \boxed{\frac{3}{\sqrt{7}}}.
